# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# Frontend (ui/)
node_modules/
ui/dist/

# Tauri generated schemas
crates/acter-app/gen/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# E2E failure screenshots, written on demand by the wdio runner
e2e/screenshots/
.claude/
.vscode/

# Scratch: a PR body being drafted, never part of the tree.
.pr-body.md

# Where a development build keeps its settings (spec 26, decision 3): the folder Acter
# was started from, which for `cargo run` and `tauri dev` is inside this tree. It holds
# somebody's own saved connections and accepted host keys, so it is theirs and not the
# repository's.
settings/

# The version the release workflow hands to `tauri build`, written from the tag (spec 26,
# amendment M). It is a build artifact of a release run, not a file anybody edits.
release-version.json

# What a release run leaves beside the repository: the folder the zip is made from, and the
# zip itself. Both are built by the workflow and neither is anybody's source.
portable-package/
acter-*-portable.zip
